    """
# NOTE:========================================================================
# Looks like every sklearn model ..., BUT INTERNALLY IT BEHAVES VERY DIFFERENT]
# =============================================================================

  |> [ What happens Inside `fit()` ]
     - Suppose you call 
        """ model.fit(X_train, y_train) """
     - In XGBoost: internally, it does:
        """
          Initialize Trees
            |
          Build Tree 1
            |
            Compute Residuals
            | 
          Build Tree 2
            |
          ....
            |
          Handred of trees created sequencially
        """
     - In MLP
        """
          Initialize Weights
              |
          Forward Pass
              |
            Loss
              |
          Backpropagation
              |
          Update Weights
              |
          Repeat 500 epochs
        """
        Again ...
        training.
     - IN 'TabICLv2': Something much simpler happens
        """ model.fit(X_train, y_train) """
        -> Internally, it mostly:
            . Stores the training dataset
            . performs preprocessing
            . downloads the pretrained checkpoint if needed 
            . optionally builds a 'KV(Key-Value) cache' for faster 
              repeated predictions
        -> 'It does not retrain The transformer on your data', The actual 
           in-context reasoning happens when you later call `predict()`
    
  |> [ Where Does learning happen? ] 
     - The answer suprises almost eveyone
     - learning happens here:
        """
          model.predict(X_test)
        """
        Not because the weights change ...
        but because the transformer receives
        """
          Training Examples
            +
          Test Example
        """
      -> at the same time.
     - Conceptually, the model is doing something like:
       """
        Transformer(
          X_train,
          y_train,
          X_test
        )
       """
       . instead of:
       """
        Transformer(X_test)
       """
       -> The training set becomes part of the input (the context), not
          something used to optimize the models parameters
        """
              Fit
               ↓
          Store X_train
            
          Store y_train
               ↓
             Predict
               ↓
             Combine

             X_train
             y_train
             X_test
               ↓
        Run ONE Transformer Forward Pass
               ↓
            Predictions
        """
      - Notice What's missing: There is 'no'
        . optimizer
        . epochs 
        . backpropagation
        . weight updates
      - during normal inference

